(7608425, 1230549, 86447, '<td valign="top">I love this one, Alex!<br/> <br/>(Thought I said so during voting, but I don''t see it.)<br/> <br/>It was my favorite of all of the bunch.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your RIBBON!<br/></td>', 'I love this one, Alex! (Thought I said so during voting, but I don''t see it.) It was my favorite of all of the bunch. Congratulations on your RIBBON!', '2019-01-14 12:12:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608428, 1230534, 114969, '<td valign="top">Great fun Gaby! I love the composition and the vivid colors. I bet it was also good fun shooting the lovely models :) Congrats on the well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'Great fun Gaby! I love the composition and the vivid colors. I bet it was also good fun shooting the lovely models :) Congrats on the well deserved ribbon!', '2019-01-14 12:24:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608459, 1230526, 109387, '<td valign="top">What a perfect take for the challenge. I really love this image Anita! The expression of the man, the flow of the water, the child floating in the air. Congrats!</td>', 'What a perfect take for the challenge. I really love this image Anita! The expression of the man, the flow of the water, the child floating in the air. Congrats!', '2019-01-14 14:58:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608483, 1230526, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Anita. Superb photo that really captures a special moment. You are brave to take photos of strangers - I am a bit wary of taking photos of strangers without their permission especially when kids are in the mix. Guess it is a sad state the world is in these days though having said that I wouldn''t want a stranger taking a photo of me and my daughter. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/> I totally agree with you Paul, its much easier being a female photographer these days</td>', 'Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Congrats Anita. Superb photo that really captures a special moment. You are brave to take photos of strangers - I am a bit wary of taking photos of strangers without their permission especially when kids are in the mix. Guess it is a sad state the world is in these days though having said that I wouldn''t want a stranger taking a photo of me and my daughter.    I totally agree with you Paul, its much easier being a female photographer these days', '2019-01-14 19:35:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608506, 1230129, 86447, '<td valign="top">She''s so beautiful, Mary!<br/> <br/>You are blessed.  I can see her happiness!<br/> <br/>I wish there were a bit more contrast... deeper blacks.<br/> <br/>But, it might just be me.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your HM!</td>', 'She''s so beautiful, Mary! You are blessed.  I can see her happiness! I wish there were a bit more contrast... deeper blacks. But, it might just be me. Congratulations on your HM!', '2019-01-14 20:51:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608513, 1230534, 86447, '<td valign="top">I hope my suggestion will not offend you, Gaby.<br/> <br/>I wish that the view from the hole were darker... with shadows coming up on the dogs.<br/> <br/>In my opinion, the under side of the hole would all be dark.   We''re looking up from a hole, right?  And holes are dark?<br/> <br/>So... the underside of the soil would not be seen.  And there would be shadows under the dogs''s chins.   Maybe just a hint of detail in the soil?<br/> <br/>I dunno... I''m just speculating.<br/> <br/>I still think the image is totally adorable and fun!<br/></td>', 'I hope my suggestion will not offend you, Gaby. I wish that the view from the hole were darker... with shadows coming up on the dogs. In my opinion, the under side of the hole would all be dark.   We''re looking up from a hole, right?  And holes are dark? So... the underside of the soil would not be seen.  And there would be shadows under the dogs''s chins.   Maybe just a hint of detail in the soil? I dunno... I''m just speculating. I still think the image is totally adorable and fun!', '2019-01-14 21:07:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608518, 1230556, 86447, '<td valign="top">I think your "flaw" was making the tower of chocolate so believable.<br/> <br/>Dang it.<br/> <br/>It probably cost you some vote points.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I think your "flaw" was making the tower of chocolate so believable. Dang it. It probably cost you some vote points. ', '2019-01-14 21:15:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608558, 1230556, 97225, '<td valign="top">Oh my goodness, Emilie is 4?! It doesn''t seem long since she was a new babe. Congratulations on the HM. This photo will always be a treasure. Great work, I love that you let her get messy.</td>', 'Oh my goodness, Emilie is 4?! It doesn''t seem long since she was a new babe. Congratulations on the HM. This photo will always be a treasure. Great work, I love that you let her get messy.', '2019-01-15 01:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7608562, 1230534, 141319, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I hope my suggestion will not offend you, Gaby.<br/> <br/>I wish that the view from the hole were darker... with shadows coming up on the dogs.<br/> <br/>In my opinion, the under side of the hole would all be dark.   We''re looking up from a hole, right?  And holes are dark?<br/> <br/>So... the underside of the soil would not be seen.  And there would be shadows under the dogs''s chins.   Maybe just a hint of detail in the soil?<br/> <br/>I dunno... I''m just speculating.<br/> <br/>I still think the image is totally adorable and fun! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not offended at all Lyda! Thank you for taking the time to crit and write. I was running out of time, when I was working on it in post I thought it would have been better to photograph the inside of a tube of some type instead of the flat surface. That would have given the feeling of the "hole" much better. Hindsight and all that :-). <br/> <br/>I was using a flash to photograph the dogs, I tried without it, but it was too dark or the sky was totally blown. Also the fuzzy coat is very unforgiving with lower shutter speeds, I mean really unforgiving :-). This being dpc I know how much a sharp image is valued ;-). Maybe I should have used a reflector on the bottom and used a flash from the top? Never thought about that before. <br/> <br/>thanks for your comments, can''t say I disagree with what you said :-). <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I hope my suggestion will not offend you, Gaby. I wish that the view from the hole were darker... with shadows coming up on the dogs. In my opinion, the under side of the hole would all be dark.   We''re looking up from a hole, right?  And holes are dark? So... the underside of the soil would not be seen.  And there would be shadows under the dogs''s chins.   Maybe just a hint of detail in the soil? I dunno... I''m just speculating. I still think the image is totally adorable and fun!   Not offended at all Lyda! Thank you for taking the time to crit and write. I was running out of time, when I was working on it in post I thought it would have been better to photograph the inside of a tube of some type instead of the flat surface. That would have given the feeling of the "hole" much better. Hindsight and all that :-).  I was using a flash to photograph the dogs, I tried without it, but it was too dark or the sky was totally blown. Also the fuzzy coat is very unforgiving with lower shutter speeds, I mean really unforgiving :-). This being dpc I know how much a sharp image is valued ;-). Maybe I should have used a reflector on the bottom and used a flash from the top? Never thought about that before.  thanks for your comments, can''t say I disagree with what you said :-).  ', '2019-01-15 01:15:19.000000', NULL, 0),
